# {{ project.name }} – freya

The user interface of this project uses **freya** (https://freyaui.dev), a
declarative Rust GUI library powered by Skia, made by Marc Espín
(https://github.com/marc2332/freya, MIT license).

**freya is an independent project. It has nothing to do with Freya TDE** –
despite the similar name, Freya TDE is neither part of freya nor made, endorsed
or supported by its authors. Freya TDE only supports freya as one of its UI
backends. Questions about freya itself belong to its own project.

## How Freya TDE uses freya

- `src/<form>.gen.rs` (generated, read-only) holds the form state, a `Message`
  per input and the view, built with freya's elements and components in the
  module `freya_ui`. Every widget is a field `crate::app::Control<T>`; your
  handlers in `src/<form>.rs` change these fields and freya renders again.
- `src/app.gen.rs` holds the shared helpers (`Control`, `FreyaRoot`, …). The
  `freya_…` names there belong to Freya TDE, not to freya.
- The first form is the main window.

## Run

```sh
cargo run
```

The first build downloads Skia binaries for freya (network needed once).

